1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,070
Listen to part of a radio program about nature.

2
00:00:03,070 --> 00:00:09,030
The camel is an example of an animal that is especially adapted to survive in harsh conditions.

3
00:00:09,030 --> 00:00:11,290
First of all, camels have humps on their backs.

4
00:00:11,290 --> 00:00:15,420
Now many people think that camels hold water in their humps

5
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:17,220
But that is actually not true.

6
00:00:17,220 --> 00:00:19,900
While camels do have to store water

7
00:00:20,320 --> 00:00:23,140
what they carry in their humps is not water but fat.

8
00:00:23,140 --> 00:00:27,290
That's their emergency supply of energy in case there's little food to eat.

9
00:00:27,290 --> 00:00:31,220
Of course camels wouldn't need to carry a safety supply of fat

10
00:00:31,220 --> 00:00:34,070
if it were easy to find something to eat where they live.

11
00:00:34,070 --> 00:00:41,010
Unfortunately in a desert, camels can sometimes walk for days in the hot sun looking for food and water.

12
00:00:41,010 --> 00:00:42,380
So when there is little to eat

13
00:00:42,440 --> 00:00:46,159
the fat from their hump allows them to survive for quite a long time,

14
00:00:46,159 --> 00:00:48,120
even up to two weeks without eating anything.

15
00:00:48,120 --> 00:00:51,320
When they do get an opportunity to eat and drink

16
00:00:51,560 --> 00:00:53,280
camels consume as much as possible.

17
00:00:53,280 --> 00:00:56,540
A camel can drink incredible amounts of water

18
00:00:56,540 --> 00:01:00,100
a lot more than most other animals can take in without getting sick.

19
00:01:00,100 --> 00:01:03,200
You see, there's a limit on how much an animal can drink.

20
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:06,300
If an animal were to drink more than necessary

21
00:01:06,860 --> 00:01:09,120
that could even be bad for that animal's health.

22
00:01:09,120 --> 00:01:13,090
But a camel's body does not suffer the effects of too much water.

23
00:01:13,090 --> 00:01:15,820
After it has stored up plenty of food and water

24
00:01:16,360 --> 00:01:18,260
it can go on for days in a hot desert.
